{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794398682,"nonce":"hgxM/7y3oaKB7HomoLle9HE46NI=","title":"Interpreter and hybrid never finalize an abstract whose native side roots a Haxe closure","message":"Reported by the hxn project. An abstract allocated with `hl_gc_alloc_gen(\u0026hlt_abstract, 16, MEM_KIND_FINALIZER)` whose native side holds `hl_add_root` on a Haxe closure, and whose finalizer calls `hl_remove_root`, is never finalized under `--mode interp` or the default hybrid mode, even though the closure cannot reach the abstract. Under `--mode jit` and stock HashLink 1.15.0 the same program finalizes them. Abstracts without a root finalize in all three modes.\n\nReproduced here on release ash at 2026-11-11 (Mac, load ~6). Output of the first line of the program, \"live after 5 collections of 2000 each\" (expected 200, the ones still held):\n\n- ash (hybrid): 10200\n- ash --mode interp: 10200, and after `held = null` + two more major collections still 10250 live\n- ash --mode jit: 200, and 51 after dropping the held ones\n\nThe last line of the program (closures that DO reach their own rooting handle) leaks by design in every mode: root -\u003e closure -\u003e box -\u003e handle.\n\nThe closures come from a function of their own that holds nothing else, so the interpreter's closure or the frame that made it is retaining something that reaches the array of abstracts, and the root makes that permanent. Cause not confirmed.\n\nHaxe source (Kept.hx; `Native` is `@:hlNative(\"counter\")` with `keep(f:Int-\u003eNull\u003cInt\u003e):hl.Abstract\u003c\"hxn_kept\"\u003e`, `call_kept`, `kept_live`):\n\n```haxe\nstatic function make(count:Int):Array\u003cRawKept\u003e {\n\treturn [for (i in 0...count) Native.keep(adder(i))];\n}\nstatic function adder(i:Int):Int-\u003eNull\u003cInt\u003e {\n\tvar own = [i, i * 2];\n\treturn value -\u003e value + own[0] + own[1];\n}\nstatic function churn(count:Int) { make(count); }\nstatic function garbage() {\n\tvar junk = [];\n\tfor (i in 0...20000) junk.push([i, i + 1, i + 2]);\n}\nstatic function main() {\n\tvar held = make(200);\n\tfor (round in 0...5) { churn(2000); garbage(); hl.Gc.major(); }\n\t// ... call_kept on each held one, then print Native.kept_live()\n}\n```\n\nNative side: `keep` does `KEPT += 1; manage(Kept(Root::new(f)))` where `Kept`'s Drop does `KEPT -= 1` and the root is removed by the abstract's finalizer; `kept_live` returns KEPT.\n\nA runnable copy (kept.hl, counter.hdll, Kept.hx, native tail) was in the scratchpad of the session that reproduced it; rebuild from the hxn repo if it is gone. Run from the directory holding the hdll: `DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH=\"$PWD:\u003cash\u003e/target/release\" ash --mode interp kept.hl`.\n\nRelated but different: c534f4d (interpreter roots missing, the opposite direction), 99ddee2 (finalizer-owned native memory stays resident a cycle longer).","files":null}]}